DTSTAMP:20260901T204343Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: European Cultural Foundation: Artistic Research Fellowshi
 p (ECF Historical Archives)
DESCRIPTION:The European Cultural Foundation invites artists to research it
 s historical archives\, held at the Historical Archives of the European Un
 ion in Florence\, through a new Artistic Research Fellowship with a EUR 10
 \,000 grant covering travel\, accommodation\, and living costs\; the artis
 tic output is delivered within two years. A strong fit for archive-driven\
 , research-based\, and critical data practices. Deadline 30 September 2026
 \, 17:00 CET. ELIGIBILITY: professional creatives in visual arts\, perform
 ing arts\, film and audiovisual practices\, podcasting and audio storytell
 ing\, documentary\, journalism or literary practices\, who can demonstrate
  a research-based practice and a clear dissemination strategy. Application
 s and all supporting documentation must be in English\, submitted via the 
 online form. Fellows work at the HAEU inside the scholarly community of th
 e European University Institute\, with the archives housed at Villa Salvia
 ti. A parallel Academic Research Fellowship of EUR 5\,000\, for PhD and po
 stdoctoral researchers\, early-career researchers within ten years of thei
 r master's or doctorate\, and independent scholars\, is listed separately 
 on the desk and shares this deadline.\n\nOrganisation: European Cultural F
 oundation\nLocation: Archives held at the Historical Archives of the Europ
 ean Union\, Florence\, Italy. Open to artists able to work with the archiv
 es.\nAward: EUR 10\,000 artistic-research grant covering travel\, accommod
 ation\, and living costs\; output delivered within 2 years. No application
  fee.\nDuration: Research fellowship in the ECF historical archives\; outp
 ut within two years.\n\nMore: https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/new
 -fellowship-programme-to-research-the-ecf-historical-archives/?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/new-fellowship-programme-to-re
 search-the-ecf-historical-archives/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Archives held at the Historical Archives of the European Union\, F
 lorence\, Italy. Open to artists able to work with the archives.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:scuola-piccola-zattere-international-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T204343Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260905
SUMMARY:Deadline: Scuola Piccola Zattere: International Fellowship and Resi
 dency 2027 (Venice)
DESCRIPTION:Scuola Piccola Zattere is an independent non-profit centre for 
 continuous education and research in the expanded field of contemporary ar
 ts\, running exhibitions\, commissions\, fellowships\, workshops\, seminar
 s\, performances and public discussions as one connected research ecosyste
 m rather than separate strands. Two international fellowships are offered.
  The support is unusually solid for a research fellowship: EUR 5\,000 as a
  grant\, EUR 2\,000 as a research budget\, accommodation\, travel and a st
 udy space for three months. SEASON THEME: the 2026-2027 cycle is titled Li
 ving Document\, investigating archives\, regulatory documents\, collective
  rituals\, games\, performative instructions\, and the relationship betwee
 n bodies\, architecture and social organisation. Fellows join that shared 
 inquiry while continuing their own work\, and are expected to keep an acti
 ve presence in the institution and contribute to public events through wor
 kshops\, seminars\, presentations\, screenings or performances. The fellow
 ship overlaps with the run-up to and opening of the 2027 Architecture Bien
 nale\, which is a real advantage if your research benefits from that traff
 ic. ELIGIBILITY: artists\, curators\, researchers\, architects\, choreogra
 phers\, performers and writers of any nationality\, as individuals\, colle
 ctives or duos. Good English is required\, and non-EU applicants need a va
 lid passport for international travel. No age limit\, but the organisers s
 ay it is especially intended for practitioners in the post-academic stage 
 of their career\, typically under 40. You must be prepared to spend the fu
 ll period in Venice\, so this is not a remote or partial-attendance fellow
 ship. WHAT THEY WANT: an active research process that can develop through 
 discussion and experimentation\, tied to the Living Document theme\, not a
  finished stand-alone project proposal. The motivation letter\, portfolio 
 and public programming proposal are read as one integrated application. De
 adline 4 September 2026 at 10:00 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: Scuola Piccola Zat
 tere\nLocation: Venice\, Italy. Open to any nationality.\nAward: EUR 5\,00
 0 fellowship grant plus a EUR 2\,000 research budget\, accommodation in Ve
 nice\, an individual study space within a shared studio\, and round-trip t
 ravel to Venice. Collectives and duos share a single grant and one accommo
 dation. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months\, in one of two slots:
  early January to early April 2027\, or mid-April to mid-July 2027. Applic
 ants may name one slot or indicate availability for both.\n\nMore: https:/
 /scuolapiccolazattere.com/en/events/internationalfellowship-2-3?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://scuolapiccolazattere.com/en/events/internationalfellowship-2-3?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Venice\, Italy. Open to any nationality.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ecf-academic-research-fellowship-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T204343Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: European Cultural Foundation: Academic Research Fellowshi
 p (ECF Historical Archives)
DESCRIPTION:The academic track of the ECF Fellowship Programme\, which fost
 ers new research engaging with the history of the European Cultural Founda
 tion and the broader role of culture in European integration. The ECF was 
 established in 1954 by figures including Denis de Rougemont\, Robert Schum
 an\, Hendrik Brugmans and Prince Bernhard of the Netherlands\, on the beli
 ef that Europe will not be built by treaties alone. Over seventy years it 
 has produced programmes\, institutes\, campaigns and collaborations\, incl
 uding a contribution to shaping and implementing the ERASMUS student mobil
 ity scheme. That legacy is now preserved at the Historical Archives of the
  European Union in Florence alongside the records of the EU's main institu
 tions\, a placement that itself recognises the Foundation's role in Europe
 an integration. ELIGIBILITY for the Academic Research Fellowship: research
 ers in European studies\, cultural studies\, history and related fields ac
 ross the humanities and social sciences\, specifically PhD and postdoctora
 l researchers\, early-career researchers within ten years of completing a 
 master's or doctoral degree\, and independent scholars with an active rese
 arch profile. Fellows work at the HAEU embedded in the international schol
 arly community of the European University Institute\, with the archives ho
 used at Villa Salviati. Applications and all supporting documentation must
  be submitted in English through the online form. NOTE: this is the EUR 5\
 ,000 academic track. The EUR 10\,000 Artistic Research Fellowship\, open t
 o professional creatives in visual arts\, performing arts\, film and audio
 visual practices\, podcasting and audio storytelling\, documentary\, journ
 alism and literary practices\, is listed separately on the desk and shares
  the same deadline.\n\nOrganisation: European Cultural Foundation\, hosted
  at the Historical Archives of the European Union\nLocation: Historical Ar
 chives of the European Union\, Villa Salviati\, Florence\, Italy\, within 
 the European University Institute.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 grant to support a r
 esearch stay at the HAEU\, covering travel\, accommodation and living expe
 nses. The parallel Artistic Research Fellowship carries EUR 10\,000 and ad
 ditionally covers artistic production. No application fee.\nDuration: Rese
 arch stay at the HAEU. Outcomes must be completed and publicly presented o
 r published within two years of signing the Grant Agreement. Deadline 30 S
 eptember 2026 at 17:00 CET.\n\nMore: https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-ca
 lls/new-fellowship-programme-to-research-the-ecf-historical-archives/?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/new-fellowship-programme-to-re
 search-the-ecf-historical-archives/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Historical Archives of the European Union\, Villa Salviati\, Flore
 nce\, Italy\, within the European University Institute.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:vcca-germaine-poliakov-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T204343Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: VCCA Germaine Poliakov Fellowship 2027
DESCRIPTION:An 18-day writing residency at le Moulin a Nef\, VCCA's site in
  the village of Auvillar in southwest France\, with a USD 1\,000 travel st
 ipend attached. The fellowship was established in 2022 by VCCA Fellow and 
 board member Sandell Morse in memory of Germaine Poliakov\, a WWII Resista
 nce worker who sheltered and cared for Jewish refugee children in a secret
  house in southwest France\, so the history of the region is bound up with
  the award itself. HARD ELIGIBILITY GATE: this is open ONLY to writers who
  are already VCCA Fellows\, meaning you must have completed a residency at
  VCCA in Virginia before you can apply. If you have never been to Mt. San 
 Angelo\, this one is closed to you for now and the route in is the Virgini
 a application first. HOW TO APPLY: there is no separate form. Complete the
  'Moulin a Nef Residencies\, VCCA in France 2027' application and indicate
  your fellowship interest in the follow-up to Question 15. A USD 30 applic
 ation fee applies. Residency dates are drawn from a long window running 15
  March to 9 December 2027\, and notification is by 15 December 2026\, so p
 lan on a roughly 15-month lead time between applying and the latest possib
 le stay.\n\nOrganisation: Virginia Center for the Creative Arts (VCCA)\nLo
 cation: le Moulin a Nef\, Auvillar\, France\, VCCA's residency site in Gas
 cony.\nAward: USD 1\,000 travel stipend on top of a fully funded 18-day re
 sidency at le Moulin a Nef. Application fee USD 30.\nDuration: 18 days\, s
 cheduled inside the 15 March to 9 December 2027 window. Applications open 
 1 June 2026\, deadline 15 September 2026\, notification by 15 December 202
 6.\n\nMore: https://www.vcca.com/apply/fully-funded-fellowships/germaine-p
 oliakov-fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://www.vcca.com/apply/fully-funded-fellowships/germaine-poliakov-f
 ellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:le Moulin a Nef\, Auvillar\, France\, VCCA's residency site in Gas
 cony.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
